These exported types are output types (`z.infer`), but the schemas accept more permissive inputs thanks to `.default(...)` (e.g., `{}` for data/ui). To avoid consumers fighting the type system when constructing configs, consider also exporting input types (e.g., `export type ObjectQLCapabilitiesInput = z.input<typeof ObjectQLCapabilitiesSchema>` and similarly for UI/OS/Stack) and using those for configuration objects.
```suggestion
export type ObjectStackCapabilities = z.infer<typeof ObjectStackCapabilitiesSchema>;

// More permissive input types for configuration objects (before defaults are applied)
export type ObjectQLCapabilitiesInput = z.input<typeof ObjectQLCapabilitiesSchema>;
export type ObjectUICapabilitiesInput = z.input<typeof ObjectUICapabilitiesSchema>;
export type ObjectOSCapabilitiesInput = z.input<typeof ObjectOSCapabilitiesSchema>;
export type ObjectStackCapabilitiesInput = z.input<typeof ObjectStackCapabilitiesSchema>;
```

These helpers rely on `any` and `capability: string`, which removes compile-time safety and makes typos easy. Consider making this generic over `subsystem` and using `keyof ObjectStackCapabilities[TSubsystem]` (and/or narrowing to boolean-valued keys) so callers can only request valid capability names without casting.
```suggestion
 * Helper types: Extract boolean-valued capability keys
 */
type BooleanKeys<T> = {
  [K in keyof T]: T[K] extends boolean ? K : never;
}[keyof T];

/**
 * Helper: Check if a specific capability is enabled
 */
export function hasCapability<
  TSubsystem extends keyof ObjectStackCapabilities,
  TCapability extends BooleanKeys<ObjectStackCapabilities[TSubsystem]>
>(
  capabilities: ObjectStackCapabilities,
  subsystem: TSubsystem,
  capability: TCapability
): boolean {
  const subsystemCaps = capabilities[subsystem];
  return subsystemCaps?.[capability] === true;
}

/**
 * Helper: Get all enabled capabilities for a subsystem
 */
export function getEnabledCapabilities<
  TSubsystem extends keyof ObjectStackCapabilities
>(
  capabilities: ObjectStackCapabilities,
  subsystem: TSubsystem
): BooleanKeys<ObjectStackCapabilities[TSubsystem]>[] {
  const subsystemCaps = capabilities[subsystem];

  // Object.keys returns string[], so we narrow it to the keys of the subsystem
  const keys = Object.keys(subsystemCaps) as (keyof typeof subsystemCaps)[];

  return keys.filter(
    (key) => subsystemCaps[key] === true
  ) as BooleanKeys<ObjectStackCapabilities[TSubsystem]>[];
```
